From: luckfox-linux <build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] env: mtd: do not put an MTD device that was never got

env_mtd_load() jumps to a label that calls put_mtd_device() before
mtd_env has been assigned, so when setup_mtd_device() fails the driver
dereferences an uninitialised pointer:

  Loading Environment from MTD... *** Warning - get_mtd_device_nm() failed
  BUG at drivers/mtd/mtdcore.c:898/__put_mtd_device()!
  BUG!
  resetting ...

setup_mtd_device() has already called env_set_default() at that point, so
the failure is meant to be recoverable: U-Boot should come up on the
built-in environment. Instead the board resets, and does so on every
boot, which turns a missing or unreadable env partition into an
unbootable system.

Free the buffer and return the error without touching the device.

Signed-off-by: luckfox-linux <build@localhost>
---
 env/mtd.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/env/mtd.c b/env/mtd.c
index b26ee809..6e6ba2c7 100644
--- a/env/mtd.c
+++ b/env/mtd.c
@@ -157,7 +157,7 @@ static int env_mtd_load(void)
 
 	ret = setup_mtd_device(&mtd_env);
 	if (ret)
-		goto out;
+		goto out_free;
 
 	sect_size = mtd_env->erasesize;
 
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@ static int env_mtd_load(void)
 out:
 	put_mtd_device(mtd_env);
 
+out_free:
 	free(buf);
 
 	return ret;
-- 
